---
title: "Tooltips"
---

Tooltips can be set for cells and column headers.

## Cell Tooltips

Use `tooltip: true` for the common case where the tooltip should match the displayed cell value. This uses `valueFormatted` when present, otherwise `value`, regardless of whether the value came from `field` or `valueGetter`. A string value shows fixed text instead.

{% apiDocumentation source="column-properties/properties.json" section="tooltips" names=["tooltip"] /%}

{% gridExampleRunner title="Cell Tooltips" name="tooltips" /%}

`tooltip: false` disables cell tooltip content supplied by `tooltip`, `tooltipField`, or `tooltipValueGetter`. Tooltips supplied at runtime by a Cell Renderer using `setTooltip`, and grid-owned validation or formula error tooltips, remain available and use the column's `tooltipComponent` and `tooltipComponentParams` when configured.

## Header Tooltips

`headerTooltip` accepts the same value forms. With `headerTooltip: true`, the displayed header name is used. Column groups accept `headerTooltip` too.

{% apiDocumentation source="column-properties/properties.json" section="tooltips" names=["headerTooltip"] /%}

{% gridExampleRunner title="Header Tooltips" name="header-tooltips" /%}

Setting `headerTooltip: false` does not disable a tooltip supplied at runtime by a custom Header Component using `setTooltip`.

## Tooltip Callback

Pass a callback to `tooltip` or `headerTooltip` to generate content dynamically. Cell callbacks can also access the row's data; header callbacks receive column/header information. Both use `TooltipCallbackParams`: `value` is the underlying cell value or displayed header name, and `valueFormatted` contains the formatted value when available.

In the example below:

- The Athlete tooltip shows another field of the same row, the country.
- The Year tooltip derives its text from the cell value.
- The Sport column header uses a `headerTooltip` callback.

{% gridExampleRunner title="Tooltip Callback" name="tooltip-callback" /%}

